GitHub Issue:
Post Date: 2017-03-19T15:15:33Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: InnerjoinAndSelect returns undefined
Description: Hello,

I have a many to one relation. Every photo has one photoCollectionId and photoCollection and every PhotoCollection has an array of Photo. Now I want to load a collection with its photos:
```typescript
 let collection = await this.collectionRepository.findOneById(id
        , {
          alias: "collection",
          innerJoinAndSelect: {
            "photos": "collection.photos"
          }
        });
```
When there is no photo related to the collection this returns undefined. However, if there is a related photo, it works as expected. 

For now I have worked around the issue like this:
```typescript
@Get("/:id/photos")
  async getOne( @Param("id") id: number) {
    let photo = await this.photoRepository.findOne({ photoCollectionId: id });
    if (photo) {
      let collection = await this.collectionRepository.findOneById(id
        , {
          alias: "collection",
          innerJoinAndSelect: {
            "photos": "collection.photos"
          }
        });
      console.log(collection);
      return collection;
    }
    else {
      let collection = await this.collectionRepository.findOneById(id);
      console.log(collection);
      return collection;
    }
  }
```

However, this is probably not how it should be I suppose. Is there a better/easier way to do this?

